{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793600461123361005,"compiled_state":{"alias":"rapid-floatable-raptors","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"34878c73f80bd2a91863e51459cae089025b44d3b7296d3b5566d62f084a109d","event_uuid":"4b4fe2c0-5e89-40f5-93fb-3ceb3358a32a","position":{"commit_sha":"f21b901fd0f5d25a564a616ed51cabc93c84f245","position":"1793594800539950224-4b4fe2c0-5e89-40f5-93fb-3ceb3358a32a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"e98ed669d2550c7f69db9b715419946e4a62c61a6aafc39998f2d274679d6b9a","event_uuid":"948985da-125c-4bfa-95a0-39fde8f7af57","position":{"commit_sha":"58f72408c61ad3b92e06e1e03404a3e7cc9e6e48","position":"1793594811598044091-948985da-125c-4bfa-95a0-39fde8f7af57"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793594800539950224,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"948985da-125c-4bfa-95a0-39fde8f7af57","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"f10f-c24a-3cfa-449e"}],"description":"## What is wrong\n\nThe `[non-codebase]` acceptance-criterion exemption is silently inert when the tag is written in backticks, and rebar's own guidance text teaches the backticked form.\n\nThe detector is `_OPERATOR_ATTESTED_TAG_RE` in `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_operator_attested.py:49`:\n\n```python\nr\"^\\s*-\\s*\\[[ xX]?\\]\\s*\\[(?:non-codebase|operator-attested)\\]\\s*(.+?)\\s*$\"\n```\n\nIt requires the tag as a bare bracketed literal immediately after the checkbox. Measured directly:\n\n```\n- [ ] `[non-codebase]` An operator applies ...   -> no match\n- [ ] [non-codebase] An operator applies ...     -> match\n```\n\n`ensure_ac_boxes_checked` (`src/rebar/_commands/txn.py:504`) filters its offender list through that regex, so a backticked tag exempts nothing and the close is refused with the tagged item listed as unchecked. The refusal message then advises \"Items with done-evidence outside the snapshot may be tagged [non-codebase] to exempt them from this check\" — which the author believes they already did.\n\n## Why the wrong form is the natural one\n\nBackticking a literal tag is the ordinary markdown instinct, and rebar's guidance actively prescribes it. `src/rebar/llm/completion_reconcile.py:34` instructs the author to mark the \"criterion with the exact `[non-codebase]` tag\" — rendering the tag in backticks. `det_operator_attested.py:6` and `:42` also discuss it in double-backtick form. An author who copies the tag as presented gets a criterion that looks exempt, reviews as exempt, and refuses at close.\n\nThe failure is silent at the only moment it could be caught cheaply: plan review admits the description, the gate raises nothing, and the mismatch surfaces at the close, after the work has merged.\n\n## Observed cost\n\nHit on ticket `f10f-c24a-3cfa-449e` after its change merged. The close refused on a criterion the author had tagged. Recovering it requires editing the description, which is a material edit, which voids the plan-review attestation and forces a fresh `review-plan` run — 15 to 20 minutes and a billable LLM pass, to delete two backticks.\n\n## Decision this ticket must settle\n\nWhether the tag's accepted surface widens or the guidance narrows. Widening the regex to tolerate optional surrounding backticks accepts the form the documentation already teaches. Narrowing means every guidance surface stops rendering the tag in backticks and the error message states the exact accepted form. Widening is the smaller change and fixes the descriptions already written; narrowing leaves those broken.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A test asserts the backticked form and the bare form of `[non-codebase]` resolve the same way under `_OPERATOR_ATTESTED_TAG_RE`, for both `- [ ]` and `- [x]` checkboxes.\n- [ ] A test asserts `ensure_ac_boxes_checked` does not refuse a close for an item tagged in whichever forms are accepted.\n- [ ] The same resolution is applied to the `[operator-attested]` compatibility alias, so the two tags cannot diverge.\n- [ ] Every guidance surface that renders the tag agrees with what the detector accepts: `completion_reconcile.py`, `det_operator_attested.py`, `det_advisory.py`, `coach_moves.py`, and the close-refusal message in `txn.py`.\n- [ ] The close-refusal message in `txn.py` states the exact accepted form rather than an untagged description of it.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes.\n\n## Provenance\n\nFound while closing `f10f-c24a-3cfa-449e`. The regex behaviour above was measured by importing `_OPERATOR_ATTESTED_TAG_RE` and matching both forms, not inferred from reading it.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3d6f-1f34-1a7c-4dd1","ticket_type":"bug","title":"A backticked [non-codebase] AC tag silently exempts nothing, and rebar's own guidance teaches the backticked form","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4b4fe2c0-5e89-40f5-93fb-3ceb3358a32a","948985da-125c-4bfa-95a0-39fde8f7af57"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793600461123361005,"uuid":"135068d0-fd27-4d85-a195-2a7c906c9c7e"}